@@ -130,6 +130,28 @@ The clinic publishes the veterinarians it employs with the specialties each hold
 
 **Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
 
+### Specialty directory
+
+<a id="req-vet-003"></a>
+
+Staff also ask the inverse question: which veterinarians hold a given specialty. The clinic publishes a specialty directory listing every specialty it knows, under its stored name, with the veterinarians holding it `[REQ-VET-003]`. Each of those veterinarians is shown by first name followed by last name. All specialties appear together rather than a page at a time. The page lists specialties, not the full roster, so a veterinarian holding no specialty appears nowhere on it `[REQ-VET-003]`. The directory has no entry point of its own: no page links to it, and a reader reaches it by its own address `[REQ-VET-003]`.
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given the clinic's specialties, when the specialty directory is opened, then every specialty is listed under its stored name.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty that veterinarians hold, when the directory is opened, then each holder is shown by first name followed by last name.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian appears nowhere on the page.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given every specialty the clinic knows, when the directory is opened, then all of them appear on one page, with no paging.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given any other page of the system, when it is rendered, then nothing on it links to the specialty directory.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. A specialty that no veterinarian holds is still listed, shown as held by none.
+2. Specialties, and the veterinarians under each, are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
+3. A clinic that knows no specialty yields an empty directory rather than a failure.
+4. The page carries the site navigation `REQ-SYS-001` requires, and that navigation gains no entry for the page itself.
+5. The page offers no search or filter over specialties or veterinarians (NG-9).
+
+**Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
+
