+## Scale and Load
+
+Rows are written on demand: a path appears once a slice designs against its size. A size nobody has recorded is written as unrecorded and treated as bounded, and the simplest correct form stands until the owner corrects the row.
+
+| Path | Dominant operations | Size | Access pattern | Form |
+|------|--------------------|------|----------------|------|
+| `GET /specialties.html` — the specialty directory | One read of every specialty, one cached read of every veterinarian, one in-memory pairing | Unrecorded, treated as bounded. The seed data holds three specialties and six veterinarians; one clinic's lists stay in the tens | Read-only page render; no write path exists for either list | Sort both collections, then pair each specialty with its holders. Unpaged, per `REQ-VET-003` |
